<title>USA: NYC gained 5,000 jobs in Sept - city comptroller.</title>
<headline>NYC gained 5,000 jobs in Sept - city comptroller.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York City gained a seasonally adjusted 5,000 jobs in September, reversing two months of declines, according to a report released Wednesday by city Comptroller Alan Hevesi.</p>
<p>Government gained more than 3,800, mostly from higher-than-usual September hiring by the Board of Education.</p>
<p>The private sector gained 1,200 jobs.</p>
</text>
